    </section>

    <section id="services">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="section-head">
          <h2>Service packages built around the work your team repeats.</h2>
          <p>This is not a generic chatbot subscription. EMC2Ops implements the actual operating workflows that affect leasing response, tenant experience, owner confidence, and admin capacity.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="cards">
          <article class="card">
            <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">MC</span>
            <h3><a href="/services/missed-call-recovery/">Missed Call Recovery</a></h3>
            <p>Automatically respond to missed calls with AI-powered SMS, capture intent, and route qualified leads into your booking flow.</p>
          </article>

          <article class="card">
            <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">LF</span>
            <h3><a href="/services/leasing-follow-up/">Tenant + Lead Follow-Up</a></h3>
            <p>Send personalized follow-ups across SMS and email so prospects, tenants, owners, and vendors get timely updates.</p>
          </article>

          <article class="card">
            <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">CRM</span>
            <h3><a href="/services/crm-workflow-automation/">CRM Workflow Automation</a></h3>
            <p>Sync calls, messages, notes, lead status, appointments, maintenance requests, and reminders into your CRM.</p>
          </article>

          <article class="card">
            <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">AI</span>
            <h3><a href="/services/ai-front-desk-property-management/">AI Front Desk for Property Management</a></h3>
            <p>Install AI voice, SMS, routing, and CRM workflows around the leasing and operations paths your team already runs.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="use-cases">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="section-head">
          <h2>Use cases matched to how property managers search for help.</h2>
          <p>Start with the problem your team is already trying to solve, then connect it to the right automation workflow.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="cards">
          <article class="card">
            <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">LT</span>
            <h3><a href="/use-cases/apartment-lead-tracking/">Apartment Lead Tracking</a></h3>
            <p>Capture renter source, qualification details, ownership, and CRM next steps from first inquiry through booked tour.</p>
          </article>

          <article class="card">
            <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">LF</span>
            <h3><a href="/use-cases/real-estate-lead-follow-up-automation/">Real Estate Lead Follow-Up Automation</a></h3>
            <p>Automate speed-to-lead, stale lead recovery, no-show follow-up, and stop rules when staff take over.</p>
          </article>

          <article class="card">
            <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">CRM</span>
            <h3><a href="/use-cases/real-estate-crm-follow-up-mess/">CRM Follow-Up Cleanup</a></h3>
            <p>Fix messy follow-up with cleaner ownership, stages, tasks, deduplication, and CRM logging rules.</p>
          </article>

          <article class="card">
            <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">L2L</span>
            <h3><a href="/use-cases/lead-to-lease-automation/">Lead-to-Lease Automation</a></h3>
            <p>Connect inquiry, tour, application, approval, and move-in handoff so renter next steps stay visible.</p>
          </article>

          <article class="card">
            <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">PM</span>
            <h3><a href="/use-cases/how-to-automate-property-management/">How to Automate Property Management</a></h3>
            <p>Start with one measurable workflow, define the exception path, and expand once the system proves useful.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="offer">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="big-offer">
          <div>
            <div class="eyebrow">Core offer</div>
            <h2>Your first AI front desk workflow, built around a measurable operating problem.</h2>
            <p class="lead">A done-for-you response system that turns missed calls, tenant questions, maintenance issues, and stale leasing leads into clean, trackable next steps.</p>
            <a href="/book-demo/" class="btn btn-primary">Book a 15-minute consultation</a>
          </div>

          <div class="offer-list">
            <div class="offer-item"><span class="check">✓</span><span>Missed call text-back automation with property-specific qualification questions.</span></div>
            <div class="offer-item"><span class="check">✓</span><span>AI voice or SMS assistant for leasing intake, FAQs, maintenance triage, and appointment routing.</span></div>
            <div class="offer-item"><span class="check">✓</span><span>CRM updates, pipeline tags, appointment reminders, team alerts, and tenant/owner notifications.</span></div>
            <div class="offer-item"><span class="check">✓</span><span>Reporting dashboard showing recovered leads, booked showings, response speed, and workflow volume.</span></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="proof">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="section-head">
          <h2>What the first workflow is built to improve.</h2>
          <p>The first automation should be easy to measure. EMC2Ops focuses on response speed, booked next steps, and the amount of repetitive admin work removed from property teams.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="proof-grid">
          <article class="proof-card">
            <strong>10 sec</strong>
            <p>Target response time after a missed call or inbound lead form.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="proof-card">
            <strong>24/7</strong>
            <p>Automated intake for after-hours leasing calls, tenant questions, and maintenance requests.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="proof-card">
            <strong>1 CRM</strong>
            <p>Conversations, statuses, notes, and tasks logged into your current workflow.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <ClientReviews />

    <section id="evidence">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="section-head">
          <h2>Use evidence to decide what to automate first.</h2>
          <p>Review completed client feedback, model the missed-call opportunity with your own assumptions, and compare implementation approaches before choosing a platform.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="cards">
          <article class="card"><span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">CP</span><h3><a href="/customers/">Customer proof</a></h3><p>See verified reviews, property-management story standards, and the line between delivery experience and vertical outcomes.</p></article>
          <article class="card"><span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">ROI</span><h3><a href="/resources/missed-call-recovery-roi-calculator/">Missed-call recovery calculator</a></h3><p>Estimate recovered conversations, qualified renters, tours, leases, and optional value using your own data.</p></article>
          <article class="card"><span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">VS</span><h3><a href="/compare/">Buying comparisons</a></h3><p>Compare AI front desks, call centers, custom workflows, and off-the-shelf software by operating fit.</p></article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="demo">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="section-head">
          <div class="eyebrow">Product preview</div>
          <h2>See the missed-call recovery control room in action.</h2>
          <p>This short walkthrough shows the first workflow we install: recover the call, qualify the renter, route the risky replies, and sync the CRM record.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="demo-showcase">
          <div class="demo-video-shell">
            <video
              class="demo-video"
              src="/social-assets/emc2ops-missed-call-recovery-demo-landing.mp4"
              poster="/social-assets/emc2ops-missed-call-recovery-demo-landing-poster.jpg"
              controls
              playsinline
              preload="metadata"
              aria-label="EMC2Ops missed-call recovery product demo"
            ></video>
          </div>

          <div class="workflow-panel card demo-panel">
            <div>
              <strong>Missed-call recovery pilot</strong>
              <span class="muted">Built for property managers who want the first workflow to prove ROI before a larger AI rollout.</span>
            </div>
            <ul>
              <li>Instant SMS reply after missed leasing calls</li>
              <li>Budget, move date, pets, and tour intent captured</li>
              <li>Human handoff for sensitive or uncertain replies</li>
              <li>Clean notes, tags, transcript, and next step logged to CRM</li>
            </ul>
            <a href="/book-demo/" class="btn btn-primary">Book a 15-minute consultation</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="pricing">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="section-head">
          <h2>Start with one workflow, then expand once it proves useful.</h2>
          <p>Exact scope depends on your CRM, call volume, integrations, phone/SMS setup, and compliance needs. The consultation helps identify which automation should come first.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="pricing">
          <article class="price-card">
            <h3>Launch</h3>
            <p>For a single high-friction workflow.</p>
            <a class="price price-link" href="/book-demo/">Get a Quote</a>
            <ul>
              <li>Missed call SMS workflow</li>
              <li>Basic lead qualification</li>
              <li>Email/SMS notifications</li>
              <li>1 CRM integration</li>
            </ul>
          </article>

          <article class="price-card featured">
            <h3>Growth</h3>
